SynQt is built on the Qt framework (https://www.qt.io). SynQt's own source code is
Apache-2.0, but applications built with SynQt link Qt modules and the Qt for
WebAssembly platform, and the license of each resulting binary is determined by the
Qt build used rather than by SynQt. In particular, with open source Qt the browser client
is GPLv3 and is conveyed to every visitor, so its source must be made available
under GPLv3. See docs/licensing.md for the full analysis and the obligations for
open source and commercial Qt users.

Third-party components bundled in this repository
-------------------------------------------------

doxygen-awesome-css (https://github.com/jothepro/doxygen-awesome-css), by jothepro,
licensed under the MIT License, is vendored under tools/docs-hooks/doxygen-awesome/
with its LICENSE and VERSION files. It styles the generated C++ reference on the
documentation site. It is a documentation build asset and is not linked into or
distributed with any SynQt binary.

CodeMirror (https://codemirror.net), by Marijn Haverbeke and others, licensed under
the MIT License, is vendored under tools/synqt/synqt/assets/design/vendor/ with its
LICENSE and a README naming each package and version. It is the file pane of the
design editor, which `synqt design` serves on this machine and which the
documentation site publishes at /designer/. It is a tool asset. No SynQt binary
links it, and nothing it does reaches an application built with SynQt.
